{"requirements":[{"id":"nfs-server-export","requirement":"node1 provides an NFSv4 export of /srv/nfs/shared over the dedicated storage network.","status":"satisfied","summary":"node1 is on 10.100.209.10/24, the export is restricted to the storage subnet 10.100.209.0/24, nfs-server is active and enabled, and clients directly mounted the export using NFSv4.2.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0e30f6ab65eb408f","cmd-2de9ffd7dde74e1e","cmd-c64da61d761d4323","cmd-bfe2a3c2de7e4861"]},{"id":"shared-identity-directory","requirement":"sharedops has UID and GID 4200 on all three nodes, and the shared directory is sharedops:sharedops with mode 2770.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three nodes directly report sharedops as UID/GID 4200. The exported directory and both mounted views report ownership 4200:4200 and mode 2770.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9f7b11419296401c","cmd-01c23d53762c47c4","cmd-ab28d0c94c4b4485","cmd-2de9ffd7dde74e1e","cmd-c64da61d761d4323","cmd-bfe2a3c2de7e4861"]},{"id":"client-mounts","requirement":"node2 and node3 mount node1:/srv/nfs/shared at /mnt/shared.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Both clients directly show the requested source mounted at /mnt/shared as NFSv4.2. Each mount recovered after its client's restart, confirming the setup is persistent.","evidence_ids":["cmd-c64da61d761d4323","cmd-bfe2a3c2de7e4861","cmd-4f0e0c3d82e6429d","cmd-51051c19b41944f8"]},{"id":"cross-client-sharing","requirement":"Files created by either client become available to the other while retaining ownership and permissions.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Files created as sharedops on node2 were read from node3, and files created on node3 were read from node2. Both directions directly showed sharedops:sharedops, numeric ownership 4200:4200, mode 660, and correct content. The behavior was repeated after all node restarts.","evidence_ids":["cmd-5f9fe44e40244a71","cmd-953abf5eb363439b","cmd-25004569d4984af3","cmd-242ff5121ec64628","cmd-6aec4d4f75e84f1e","cmd-761392eec1a1485f"]}],"confidence":1.0,"operational_hygiene":{"score":1.0,"summary":"No unnecessary mutations were identified. Package installation, identity creation, export and mount configuration, test-file creation, and restarts all had clear roles in implementing or directly verifying the requested outcome and mandatory restart protocol. The failed configuration attempt created the required export directory before discovering that /etc/exports.d was absent; that required state was retained and the configuration was immediately completed, so it was not an unnecessary mutation. Final lifecycle checks show no failed services and healthy package state on every node. The added NFS/RPC listeners are attributable to the required NFS service.","evidence_ids":["cmd-f707aa2229bc4c46","cmd-38d99d244fd94acd","cmd-ff63bf5beabb44bb","cmd-870d34f452094283","cmd-2de9ffd7dde74e1e","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node2:failed-services","global:after_executor:node3:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health","global:after_executor:node3:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for node1, node2, and node3: each has a healthy pre-restart observation, restart acknowledgement, changed boot identity, and recovered service, mount, identity, ownership, permissions, and shared data. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor's before/after observations.","limitations":[]}
